cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PhyloRender in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "PhyloRender: an interactive and agent-ready package for reproducible phylogenetic visualization"
license: "GPL-3.0-or-later"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/Jhe1004/PhyloRender"
url: "https://github.com/Jhe1004/PhyloRender"
abstract: >-
  PhyloRender is an open-source phylogenetic visualization package providing
  both an interactive browser workbench and a Model Context Protocol (MCP)
  server paired with a domain Agent Skill on a single shared rendering engine.
  It covers multi-support phylograms, fossil-calibrated chronograms with
  official ICS geologic timescales, cytonuclear tanglegrams, and multi-locus
  gene-tree cloudograms with built-in four-category discordance pie charts and
  penalized-likelihood visual alignment, exporting overlap-free vector SVG,
  high-DPI PNG, and monophyletic two-panel figures.
keywords:
  - chronogram
  - cloudogram
  - cytonuclear discordance
  - Model Context Protocol
  - phylogenomics
  - tanglegram
